tps://api.github.com/users/meowyih/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meowyih/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meowyih/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meowyih/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meowyih/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/meowyih/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-11-27T10:45:52Z","updated_at":"2025-11-27T10:47:28Z","body":"If you follow the steps in the video, I assumed you can come up with the exact same project as below:\n[project_1127.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/23789902/project_1127.zip)\n\nIf not, I really don't know what happen. :(\n\nWhen you open the project_1127 using Godot 4.5.1, no matter how many times you try, there is always two errors message \"ERROR: Animation 'new_animation' does not exist\" in the Output dialog at the bottom. And when clicked \"Run\" button, there is always a \"get_frame_count: Animation 'new_animation' does not exist.\" msg in the Debugging window.\n\nAlso, if you click the refresh button in the \"Animation\" property in the inspector windows for /node_3d/AnimatedSpirited3D, it will show a non-exist animation name 'new_animation' in the box. This is the root of the problem. \n\nSo this bug should be able to fix by updating the animation list to all the scenes in the Editor when there is some change.\n\nBy the way, project_1127 is the simplest MRP I can come up with. In this project, user can actually fix the error msg by deleting the old SpriteFrame and reassign again (or maybe several times using different steps). But when I found this problem, my project is more complicate and I delete/rename/create the animation too many time that cannot be simply fixed using this way.","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/358520128